  "capability": "certify_height_invariance (engine geometry-function-engine/24, no new registry primitive)",
  "proof_sketch": "Let t = h². Solid-vertex affine coordinates do not depend on t; the metric is G = G₂ ⊕ (t), so every inner product u·v = u₂ᵀG₂v₂ + t·u_z·v_z is affine in t, and every Gram matrix has the form A + t·zzᵀ, whose determinant is affine in t (matrix determinant lemma). Hence each whitelisted goal² is P(t)/Q(t) with deg P, deg Q ≤ 2 (lengths: deg 1; point–plane / line–line / line–plane / plane–plane distances: ratio of Gram determinants, deg ≤ 1 each; cos² of angles: (u·v)² / ((u·u)(v·v)), deg ≤ 2 each), and Q(t) > 0 for t > 0 (non-degenerate solid). If the goal takes the same value c at 5 distinct t, then P − cQ (degree ≤ 2, certificate bound ≤ 3) has 5 roots, so P ≡ cQ and the goal equals c for every height.",
  "proof_caveat": "Relies on (i) goal operands being solid vertices (coordinates independent of t) — enforced by guard; (ii) the same combinatorial frame at every sample (same free anchor, no mirror/flip) — enforced; (iii) exact Fraction/Radical evaluation (no floating point). Certificate field max_degree=3 is a conservative bound; 5 samples exceed it.",
  "guards": [
    "all asks in whitelist",
    "all goal labels are solid vertices",
    "all 5 samples SERVED with ≤1 free anchor",
    "identical goal signature",
    "not on mirror/flip exploration path",
    "only after MISSING_DIMENSION"
  ],
